<title>ECUADOR: Ecuador's money base up to 2.7 bln sucres Sept 6.</title>
<headline>Ecuador's money base up to 2.7 bln sucres Sept 6.</headline>
<dateline>QUITO 1996-09-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ecuador's money base rose 6.38 percent to 2.7 billion sucres in the week to September 6, the Central Bank said Monday.</p>
<p>In the previous week to August 31, the money base grew 4.1 percent.</p>
<p>The bank did not explain the increase.</p>
<p>The money base ended 1995 at 2.41 billion sucres, up from 1.85 billion sucres at the end of 1994.</p>
<p>-- Gustavo Oviedo, Quito Newsroom, 5932 258433</p>
